---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Introduction">
  <p>
    MarkRust is a fast, local-first Markdown editor for developers and technical writers.
    It reads and writes ordinary <code>.md</code> files on disk — no proprietary document format,
    no account, no cloud requirement.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-it-is">What it is</h2>
  <p>
    MarkRust renders Markdown inline as you write. Syntax delimiters hide when your cursor
    moves away; formatting appears as styled text. The file on disk remains plain Markdown.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-it-is-not">What it is not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Not a full IDE or code project manager</li>
    <li>Not a note vault with proprietary sync</li>
    <li>Not a paid editor with feature gating</li>
    <li>Not an AI-first product — it is an editor first</li>
  </ul>

  <Callout type="tip">
    <p>Open a folder. Edit Markdown. Keep the files. That is the entire workflow.</p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="next-steps">Next steps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/docs/install">Install MarkRust</a></li>
    <li><a href="/docs/first-document">Create your first document</a></li>
    <li><a href="/docs/shortcuts">Learn keyboard shortcuts</a></li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
